      "widgets_values": [
        "masterpiece, best quality, score_7, safe, \nhighres,\n\n---\n\n(artist:herohero_(higashi_no_dou):3.0),ginhaha,atdan,hoprosuke,takiki,xipa,(mignon,artist:quasarcake,artist:houkisei,artist:kedama milk,40hara:0.6),piromizu,(ke-ta:0.95),(modare:0.95),year 2024,year 2025,\n\n---\n\nA young woman in her early twenties nestles into a well-worn single-seat sofa by a rain-streaked window, her legs tucked up beneath a draped throw blanket. She has shoulder-length black hair with softly curled ends, amber-brown eyes half-lidded behind round gold-rimmed glasses that have slipped slightly down her nose. A faded red cord bracelet sits loosely on her right wrist, its color muted against her pale skin.\n\nHer expression is quiet and distant — not quite looking at anything, lips barely curved in an unconscious, gentle smile. She leans her temple against the sofa's armrest, one hand tucked under her head, the other hanging limp over the cushion edge with fingertips still loosely resting on ose is weightless, suspended somewhere between daydreaming and a nap that never quitearrived.\n\nShe wears a creamy off-white open-front knit cardigan, its sleeves slightly too long and swallowing her hands, layered over a soft grey cotton camisole with thin straps visible at the collarbone. Dark navy lounge shorts peek out beneath the hem. A sketchbook lies open across her lap, pages curling at the corner, a stray pencil resting in the crease without its cap.\n\nSeen from a slightly elevated angle as if from someone standing in the doorway, the composition frames her diagonally — the sofa anchoring the lower right, the rain-streaked window filling the upper\nleft. The window glass blurs the city outside into soft smears of grey, green, and muteside the sofa sits a half-empty ceramic mug, its contents long cold, a forgotten propin a lazy afternoon.\n\nThe light is diffuse and overcast, filtered through thick rain clouds — cool grey ambient fill with a faint silver highlight tracing the edge of her cardigan and the bridge of her glasses. No hard shadows, no direct sun, just the gentle wrap of an overcast afternoon. The texture is soft and lived-in: knit wool, worn cotton, slightly rumpled cushions, the subtle grain of rain trails on glass.\n\nThe mood is still, tender, and deeply intimate — a stolen quiet moment on a rainy weekday, the kind that asks nothing and holds everything. The color palette is muted and harmonious: oatmeal cream, heather grey, navy blue, and the washed-out green-grey of rain-soaked glass, with the single warm note of the red bracelet anchoring the whole frame. It feels like a photograph you took of someone you love without them noticing.\n\n---\n\nlight leaks,light rendering,light-rays,ray tracing,lens flare,volumetric lights,ray tracing,lens flare,see-through silhouette,\nrim lighting,volumetric lights,\nhigh-key and low-variance brightness scale,\nbokeh,blurry foreground,light particles,\nslender figure,  masterpiece, best quality, amazing quality,\n"
      ],
